{
  "program": "CBSTM03B",
  "caseId": "case12",
  "description": "The asymmetric capability matrix, and the silent no-op it produces. CUSTFILE is ACCESS MODE IS RANDOM (app/cbl/CBSTM03B.CBL:45) and 3000-CUSTFILE-PROC tests M03B-OPEN, M03B-READ-K and M03B-CLOSE - never M03B-READ. A plain 'R' against it therefore matches no IF and falls out of the third one straight into 3900-EXIT, whose MOVE CUSTFILE-STATUS TO LK-M03B-RC is outside every IF and still runs. So the call performs no I/O and returns the file's LAST-KNOWN status. The sequence makes that unmistakable: the keyed read before it leaves '23' in CUSTFILE-STATUS, so the plain read reports '23' rather than the '00' a fresh status would carry, and the record area comes back exactly as it went in.",
